  }, {
    "heading": "1-workflow-name",
    "content": "This helps keep your workspace organized, especially when you’re managing multiple workflows."
  }, {
    "heading": "2-save",
    "content": "After making changes to your workflow, you can save your progress by clicking the ‘Save’ button at the top of the screen. This ensures all your edits are stored, so you don’t lose any work."
  }, {
    "heading": "2-save",
    "content": "If you forget to save your changes and try to leave the page or navigate away, appse ai will prompt you with a pop-up asking if you want to save the changes or leave without saving. This gives you a chance to confirm and save your work before exiting."
  }, {
    "heading": "2-save",
    "content": "This feature ensures you don’t lose any progress on your workflow!"
  }, {
    "heading": "3-run-once",
    "content": "The **Run Once** button lets you **manually run the entire workflow** from start to finish, without having to activate or deploy it. This is useful for testing or previewing your workflow in its current state."
  }, {
    "heading": "3-run-once",
    "content": "When you click ‘&#x2A;*Run Once’**, appse ai executes all the nodes in the workflow, just as if it were triggered automatically. However, keep in mind that **it will still sync actual data** and could **cause changes in the connected applications**, so use it with caution."
  }, {
    "heading": "3-run-once",
    "content": "This allows you to test your workflow without fully activating it, providing flexibility to make adjustments before going live."
  }, {
    "heading": "4-inactiveactive-toggle",
    "content": "The Inactive/Active toggle is used to activate or deactivate your workflow. Clicking the toggle will switch it to Active, which means your workflow will begin continuously syncing data as per the defined triggers or schedules. Once activated, you can toggle it back to Inactive at any time to stop the automation."
  }, {
    "heading": "5-get-started",
    "content": "The **Get Started** button takes you to a **selection screen** where you can choose your **trigger node**. A trigger node defines **how** and **when** your workflow should start. You can choose from **Trigger Manually**, **On Schedule**, or **Webhook** triggers,  or **In-app triggers**, depending on your workflow needs."
  }, {
    "heading": "5-get-started",
    "content": "This step is essential to define what starts the workflow, and it gives you the flexibility to choose the most relevant trigger for your use case."
  }, {
    "heading": "6-apps",
    "content": "When you click the **Apps** button, it will open a **selection screen** where you can choose from a list of available apps.\\\nThis allows you to select the app you want to connect to and start creating a workflow based on your chosen app."
  }, {
    "heading": "6-apps",
    "content": "It’s the easiest way to integrate and automate tasks between your apps directly within the workflow designer."
  }, {
    "heading": "7-actions",
    "content": "Clicking the Action button opens a selection screen where you can choose from various action nodes.\\\nThese include nodes like &#x2A;*Trigger Manually, Webhook, On Schedule, Filter, Decision, Merge, Code, Loop, HTTP, JSON Converter, Splitter, and Base64 Decode.**"
  }, {
    "heading": "7-actions",
    "content": "These nodes define the actions and logic that shape the flow of your workflow"
  }, {
    "heading": "8-notes",
    "content": "Notes are used to **add text annotations** directly on the workflow canvas.\\\nYou can use them to write descriptions, instructions, or reminders that help explain parts of your workflow.\\\nThey don’t affect the workflow’s execution, they’re simply for documentation and better organization."
  }, {
    "heading": "9-import-workflow",
    "content": "The Import Workflow feature allows users to import workflows by uploading an encrypted &#x2A;*`.awf`** file. This makes it easy to share workflows across teams or organizations, eliminating the need to recreate them from scratch."
  }, {
    "heading": "10-export-workflow",
    "content": "The **Export Workflow*&#x2A; feature allows you to download your workflow from the Workflow Designer as an encrypted &#x2A;*`.awf`** file."
  }, {
    "heading": "10-export-workflow",
    "content": "This is particularly useful for sharing workflows across teams or organizations, enabling others to easily reuse or collaborate on the same workflow without having to recreate it. It also serves as a great way to keep a backup of your workflows for safekeeping or version control. Additionally, you can move workflows between different appse ai accounts or environments, streamlining the process of transferring workflows without the need to rebuild them from scratch."
  }, {
    "heading": "11-click-to-start",
    "content": "The **Click to Start** area encourages users to begin creating their workflow by adding a node. When you click on the **plus icon** in the center of the canvas, it takes you to a **selection screen** where you can choose the first node to start building your automation. This is the first step in designing your workflow, where you’ll define how your automation begins and set the foundation for the entire process."
  }, {
    "heading": "12-undo",
    "content": "The **Undo** button allows you to quickly **reverse** your most recent action. If you make a mistake or want to try a different approach, simply click **Undo** to revert to the previous step. This is a handy tool for experimenting with your workflow without the worry of permanent changes."
  }, {
    "heading": "13-redo",
    "content": "The **Redo** button allows you to **reinstate** an action that was previously undone. If you’ve used the Undo button and decide you want to bring back your most recent change, click **Redo** to restore it. This gives you flexibility to step forward after undoing an action, ensuring you can adjust your workflow as needed."
  }, {
    "heading": "14-zoom-in",
    "content": "The **Zoom In** button allows you to &#x2A;*increase the canvas view by 5%** each time you click it. This helps you focus on specific areas of your workflow by making the nodes and connections appear larger, allowing for a more detailed view. You can click it multiple times to zoom in progressively as needed."
  }, {
    "heading": "15-zoom-out",
    "content": "The **Zoom Out** button allows you to &#x2A;*decrease the canvas view by 5%** each time you click it. This helps you get a broader view of your workflow, making it easier to see the entire canvas and how different nodes connect. You can click it multiple times to zoom out progressively as needed."
  }, {
    "heading": "16-fit-to-screen",
    "content": "The **Fit to Screen** button automatically adjusts the canvas view to **fit the entire workflow** within the screen. This allows you to see your whole workflow at once, making it easier to get an overview of the entire process and ensure all nodes and connections are visible."
  }, {
    "heading": "17-tidy-up",
    "content": "The **Tidy Up** button automatically **arranges and aligns** the nodes on the canvas in a clean, organized layout. It ensures that your workflow is visually neat, with consistent spacing between nodes and a structured flow, making it easier to read and manage."
  }],
