export let structuredData = {
  "contents": [{
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "The **Code Node** allows you to run custom code to transform data, perform complex logic, or aggregate information that standard nodes can't handle. It provides a secure, sandboxed environment for data manipulation."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "This might be helpful in situations such as:"
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "Transforming JSON structures (e.g., renaming fields, restructuring objects)"
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "Filtering items based on complex conditions"
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "Aggregating data (e.g., summing up order totals)"
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "Merging data from multiple previous nodes"
  }, {
    "heading": "modes-of-execution",
    "content": "The Code Node operates in two modes, which determine how input data is processed:"
  }, {
    "heading": "modes-of-execution",
    "content": "**Run Once for All Items** (Default):"
  }, {
    "heading": "modes-of-execution",
    "content": "**Input**: The `$input` variable receives an **Array** of all items from the previous node."
  }, {
    "heading": "modes-of-execution",
    "content": "**Output**: Must return an **Array** of object."
  }, {
    "heading": "modes-of-execution",
    "content": "**Ideal for**: Aggregation, sorting, filtering, or merging data."
  }, {
    "heading": "modes-of-execution",
    "content": "**Run for Each Item**:"
  }, {
    "heading": "modes-of-execution",
    "content": "**Behavior**: Automatically iterates over the incoming list of items. Your code is executed once for **every** item in the payload."
  }, {
    "heading": "modes-of-execution",
    "content": "**Input**: The `$input` variable receives a **Single Object** representing the current item being processed."
  }, {
    "heading": "modes-of-execution",
    "content": "**Output**: Your code must return a **Single Object** (the transformed version of that item)."
  }, {
    "heading": "modes-of-execution",
    "content": "*Note:* Returning an Array in this mode (e.g. `return [1, 2]`) or returning the whole input array (e.g. `return $input.all()`) will trigger an error, as this mode strictly expects a single object per iteration."
  }, {
    "heading": "modes-of-execution",
    "content": "**Ideal for**: Mapping fields, formatting values, or adding new properties to items independently without writing a manual loop."
  }, {
    "heading": "language",
    "content": "Currently, the Code Node supports **JavaScript** only. You can write standard ES6+ JavaScript to manipulate your data."
  }, {
    "heading": "code",
    "content": "This is where you write your custom code for data transformation."
  }, {
    "heading": "code",
    "content": "The code must return a valid JSON output (Array or Object depending on the mode)."
  }, {
    "heading": "code-editor-features",
    "content": "The built-in code editor provides several tools to help you write and debug your logic:"
  }, {
    "heading": "code-editor-features",
    "content": "**Autocomplete**: Type `$` to see suggestions for previous nodes (e.g., `$('Get Users')`), type `$input` to access the current item's data, or start typing a variable name or method name to see suggestions for standard JavaScript methods. Suggestions from previous nodes are available once those nodes have been executed. Use `Ctrl` + `Space` for toggling the suggestion tooltip on or off."
  }, {
    "heading": "code-editor-features",
    "content": "**Code Formatting**: Use **Alt** + **Shift** + **F** to automatically format your code with proper indentation and spacing. This is a native editor feature that helps keep your transformation logic clean and readable."
  }, {
    "heading": "code-editor-features",
    "content": "**Real-time Linting**: Flags errors immediately, such as syntax issues or attempts to modify read-only data. Warnings will appear if data from previous nodes is not available — this typically means those nodes have not been executed yet."
  }, {
    "heading": "code-editor-features",
    "content": "**Console Output**: Use `console.log()` to print messages to your browser's developer console for debugging."
  }, {
    "heading": "code-editor-features",
    "content": "**Syntax Highlighting**: Colors your code for better readability."
  }, {
    "heading": "input",
    "content": "This is the main variable containing your input data."
  }, {
    "heading": "input",
    "content": "**In \"Run Once for All Items\" mode**:\r\n`$input` is an **Array** containing **all items** returned by the previous node. You have access to the entire dataset at once."
  }, {
    "heading": "input",
    "content": "*Example:* `[ { \"id\": 1, \"name\": \"Ali\" }, { \"id\": 2, \"name\": \"Bob\" } ]`"
  }, {
    "heading": "input",
    "content": "**In \"Run for Each Item\" mode**:\r\n`$input` is a **Single Object** representing **one item** from the list. The code runs individually for each item in the dataset."
  }, {
    "heading": "input",
    "content": "*Example:* `{ \"id\": 1, \"name\": \"Ali\" }` (First execution) -> `{ \"id\": 2, \"name\": \"Bob\" }` (Second execution)"
  }, {
    "heading": "inputall",
    "content": "When running in &#x2A;*\"Run for Each Item\"** mode, you can still access the entire array of all incoming items by calling `$input.all()`. This returns the full array of input objects, which is useful when you need context from other items while processing a single item."
  }, {
    "heading": "inputall",
    "content": "*Warning:* Do not return the result of `.all()` directly (e.g., `return $input.all()`) in \"Run for Each Item\" mode, as this will result in a type error. You must still return a single object representing the transformed item."
  }, {
    "heading": "node-name",
    "content": "Access output from any previous node by name regardless of the mode. In the figure above, **SAP Business One** is the node name."
  }, {
    "heading": "node-name",
    "content": "**Syntax**: `$('Node Name').all()`"
  }, {
    "heading": "node-name",
    "content": "Use `$('Node Name').all()` to retrieve the *entire array* of outputs from that specific node, instead of just the corresponding single item."
  }, {
    "heading": "node-name",
    "content": "**Example:**"
  }, {
    "heading": "steps-to-use-the-code-node",
    "content": "Select the **Code Node** from the node selection screen."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps-to-use-the-code-node",
    "content": "Connect it to a node that provides data (e.g., an HTTP Request Node or App Node)."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps-to-use-the-code-node",
    "content": "Open the **Configuration** tab and select your **Mode** (Run Once or Run Each)."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps-to-use-the-code-node",
    "content": "Write your JavaScript logic in the **Code** section. Utilize `$input` to access input data."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps-to-use-the-code-node",
    "content": "Use `console.log()` to debug if needed."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps-to-use-the-code-node",
    "content": "Click **Run** to test your code and see the output."
  }, {
    "heading": "example-calculate-total-with-tax",
    "content": "**Scenario**: You have a list of orders and want to format the date and calculate the total price including tax."
  }, {
    "heading": "example-calculate-total-with-tax",
    "content": "**Mode**: Run for Each Item"
  }, {
    "heading": "output-behavior",
    "content": "**Success**: The Output panel will show the transformed data (Array or Object depending on mode)."
  }, {
    "heading": "output-behavior",
    "content": "**Errors**: Syntax errors are pointed out in the editor itself via real-time linting (highlighted with red squiggly lines). If code with errors is executed, or if runtime exceptions occur, they will be shown in the output section. You may also find additional error details in your browser's developer console."
  }, {
    "heading": "output-behavior",
    "content": "*Type Errors:* The editor's linter will warn you if you attempt to return the wrong type of data. Most notably, **you cannot return an Array in \"Run for Each Item\" mode**. If you try to return `[ ... ]` or `$input.all()`, the linter will block it with a squiggly line."
  }, {
    "heading": "output-behavior",
    "content": "**Important**: Input data is **Read-Only**. Always return a **new** object or array. Do not directly modify `$input`, `$input.all()`, or `$('Node Name')`."
  }, {
